&lt;b&gt;POS-33475&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Senior Business Systems Analyst, Partner Systems &amp;amp; Automation&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the Team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HubSpot&#39;s Partner Systems &amp;amp; Automation team builds the systems, automations, and integrations that power HubSpot&#39;s partner ecosystem — one of the most strategically important parts of the business, representing a significant share of HubSpot revenue. We work across HubSpot&#39;s internal CRM portals, Workato, ServiceNow, Snowflake, and a range of third-party systems, and we are actively expanding our use of AI-assisted workflows to move faster from problem identification to working solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We identify problems, design solutions, build them, ship them, and own them. Our BSAs sit at the boundary between business operations and technical execution — close enough to the business to understand what matters, and technical enough to build it. We are looking for a Senior BSA who thinks like a builder, operates like an engineer, and communicates like a business partner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;In This Role, You&#39;ll Get To&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership of complex, cross-functional automation and systems work across HubSpot&#39;s Solutions Partner program — one of the most mature and technically demanding parts of our partner ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify inefficiencies and root causes across partner operations workflows, then design, build, test, and ship solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain integrations, automations, and data pipelines using Workato and HubSpot CRM, with SQL and REST APIs as standard tools of the trade&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype AI-assisted workflows and automation agents, bringing them from idea to working implementation and iterating based on real usage data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scope work rigorously — define the problem, quantify the impact, propose the right-sized solution, and know when to prototype before committing to a full build&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with stakeholders across Partner Operations, Partner Product, Engineering, Finance, and Analytics to translate business problems into technical solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Push back constructively when a request does not justify the investment, and help stakeholders understand why&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate across multiple partner program domains over time — Solutions Partners is your primary home, but this team is deliberately moving toward cross-domain capability and you will be part of that shift&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the team&#39;s technical standards and share what you learn, so useful discoveries by one person become capabilities for everyone&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;We Are Looking For Someone With&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of hands-on experience in a role where you built and shipped production systems — business systems analyst, automation engineer, internal tools engineer, or similarly technical operations role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical fluency across the systems stack — SQL, REST APIs, Python, and JSON are standard tools for you; you use them to understand, diagnose, and extend systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with iPaaS tools (Workato, Zapier, Boomi, or similar) — building and maintaining multi-step automations and integrations across complex systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with engineering hygiene for production systems — version control, incremental rollouts, and basic testing practices that make what you build safe to operate and easy for others to maintain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Either shipped an AI-assisted feature or automation that real users used, or have a strong production track record and genuine interest in applying AI to operational workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working in ambiguous environments where the right problem is not always the stated problem — you ask the questions that reframe the work before you start building&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across multiple stakeholder groups with different incentives and priorities, and the ability to align people without formal authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication — you can explain a complex system to a non-technical audience and a complex business problem to an engineer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A sense of ownership that extends past delivery — you define expected outcomes before you build, check them after you ship, and treat the systems you own as your ongoing responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
