&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;POS-12956&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HubSpot&#39;s Legal team is extremely technology-forward. Attorneys who believe that AI and great systems can transform how legal work gets done. Our Legal Technology team exists at the center of that bet: we build the AI agents, manage the systems and integrate their operational infrastructure which lets our lawyers focus on high-value legal work instead of manual process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This isn&#39;t a &quot;keep the lights on&quot; role. You&#39;ll implement AI-powered solutions, design agentic workflows, implement and own SaaS solutions heavy with AI and sit alongside AI-minded legal stakeholders. If you want to do work that matters, is visible, and drives value for in-house Legal teams with AI, this is it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead AI solution design and delivery: build, configure, and deploy AI agents and agentic workflows using tools like Claude, Cowork, ChatGPT, and Glean within and across legal applications. This is real implementation work, not exploration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the legal tech ecosystem as part of our team: serve as one of the technical SMEs across Legal SaaS applications (CLMs, Matter Management, DSAR tooling and more), driving reliability, optimization, and integration quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build integrations: design and develop workflow automations and integrations using Workato and similar iPaaS platforms, connecting legal systems to the broader HubSpot stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate business needs into technical solutions: partner directly with attorneys and legal leadership to understand workflows, surface opportunities, and deliver solutions with measurable impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive AI adoption: work alongside the legal team to identify opportunities to embed AI tools (Claude, Glean, Harvey, Workato AI, and others) into day-to-day legal workflows, and support enablement so adoption actually sticks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the roadmap: contribute to a technically feasible product roadmap, balancing strategic priorities with iterative delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and communicate value: develop KPIs and reporting to demonstrate the business impact of technology investments to senior legal leadership, including the CLO.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay ahead of the curve: monitor the rapidly evolving legal tech landscape and bring forward-looking perspective on tools, capabilities, and trends.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on technical skills: SaaS application configuration, API usage, system integration design, and workflow automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real experience building and deploying AI solutions in enterprise environments: AI agents, agentic workflows, LLM-powered tools, or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with iPaaS platforms for building integrations and automations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to operate as a technical consultant to a non-technical business audience: learn and understand business context, problem solve, and translate ambiguous needs into scoped, deliverable solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-directed, highly organized, and able to manage multiple workstreams with autonomy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communicator, equally comfortable in a Slack thread with a lawyer and a design doc with an engineer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in or with legal departments: in-house legal teams, law firms, or legal tech vendors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with legal technology applications: CLM systems, matter management, or legal service management platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with enterprise AI tools in a professional context (Claude, Glean, ChatGPT Enterprise, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
